        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Residential one- or two-family dwelling and residential condominium claims generally have a 60-day period. Claims arising under § 1311.021 for qualifying oil-and-gas work use 120 days. Other covered improvements generally use 75 days."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is the deadline counted from project completion?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Ohio Revised Code § 1311.06 measures the listed filing periods from the last labor or work performed or material furnished by the claimant."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Where do I file?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Record the affidavit with the county recorder in the county where the improved property is located."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does the affidavit need notarization?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. It is a sworn affidavit and should be executed before a notary in accordance with the statutory form and recording requirements."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Must I send the owner a copy?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Generally yes, within 30 days after filing. Preserve evidence of service and follow the statutory alternative if ordinary service cannot be completed."
      }
    }
  ]
};

